# The short proof on Windows (Maat 1.5.1): the quick suites in Git Bash, about 50 minutes in all, instead of the whole
# Windows part of the full run (about 10 hours). `bash tools/giro-completo.sh --windows-breve …` runs these lines in this
# order; each entry must be in tools/suite.list. A line: [VAR=value …] <entry>. Since 1.6.0 the real Windows proof is
# the CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml: every suite but those of the «-» lines of tools/suite-gruppi-windows.list, at every
# push); this list stays for a quick local check. Seconds measured in Git Bash in the 1.5.0 full run (machine shared).
tools/suite.test.sh
stop-hook
blocks-independent
phase-usage
session-start
harness-merge
phase-events
maat-config
context-pack
genericita
senza-wsl
maat-paths
messages
cycle-report
guard
bash-node
test-review-surface
gates
# total ≈ 2900 s (≈ 48 min): 35 10 16 19 33 47 57 70 94 125 136 200 213 232 247 248 270 826.
# 1.6.0: rollback.test.sh (the way back to the bash engine, left out of this list in 1.5.1) is gone with the bash
# engine; going back is reinstalling Maat 1.5.1 (README, «Going back to 1.5.1»).
